       These functions return the tangent of _x, where _x is given in radians.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the tangent of _x.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If  _x is positive infinity or negative infinity, a domain error occurs,
       and a NaN is returned.

       If the correct result would overflow, a range  error  occurs,  and  the
       functions  return HHUUGGEE__VVAALL, HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF, or HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively, with
       the mathematically correct sign.

